012460,000040: 
012461,000041:                                                                                          	# THIS ROUTINE TAKES THE SHAFT AND TRUNNION ANGLES AS READ BY THE CM OPTICAL SYSTEM AND CONVERTS THEM INTO A UNIT
012462,000042:                                                                                          	# VECTOR REFERENCED TO THE NAVIGATION BASE COORDINATE SYSTEM AND COINCIDENT WITH THE SEXTANT LINE OF SIGHT.
012463,000043: 
012464,000044:                                                                                          	# THE INPUTS ARE  1) THE SEXTANT SHAFT AND TRUNNION ANGLES ARE STORED SP IN LOCATIONS 3 AND 5 RESPECTIVELY OF THE
012465,000045:                                                                                          	# MARK VAC AREA.  2) THE COMPLEMENT OF THE BASE ADDRESS OF THE MARK VAC AREA IS STORED SP AT LOCATION X1 OF YOUR
012466,000046:                                                                                          	# JOB VAC AREA.
012467,000047: 
012468,000048:                                                                                          	# THE OUTPUT IS A HALF-UNIT VECTOR IN NAVIGATION BASE COORDINATES AND STORED AT LOCATION 32D OF THE VAC AREA. THE
012469,000049:                                                                                          	# OUTPUT IS ALSO AVAILABLE AT MPAC.
