012507,000087:                                                                                          	# CALCSXA COMPUTES THE SEXTANT SHAFT AND TRUNNION ANGLES REQUIRED TO POSITION THE OPTICS SUCH THAT A STAR LINE-
012508,000088:                                                                                          	# OF-SIGHT LIES ALONG THE STAR VECTOR.  THE ROUTINE TAKES THE GIVEN STAR VECTOR AND EXPRESSES IT AS A VECTOR REF-
012509,000089:                                                                                          	# ERENCED TO THE OPTICS COORDINATE SYSTEM.  IN ADDITION IT SETS UP THREE UNIT VECTORS DEFINING THE X, Y, AND Z AXES
012510,000090:                                                                                          	# REFERENCED TO THE OPTICS COORDINATE SYSTEM.
012511,000091: 
012512,000092:                                                                                          	# THE INPUTS ARE  1) THE STAR VECTOR REFERRED TO PRESENT STABLE MEMBER COORDINATES STORED AT STAR.  2) SAME ANGLE
012513,000093:                                                                                          	# INPUT AS *SMNB*, I.E. SINES AND COSINES OF THE CDU ANGLES, IN THE ORDER Y Z X, AT SINCDU AND COSCDU.  A CALL
012514,000094:                                                                                          	# TO CDUTRIG WILL PROVIDE THIS INPUT.
012515,000095: 
012516,000096:                                                                                          	# THE OUTPUTS ARE THE SEXTANT SHAFT AND TRUNNION ANGLES STORED DP AT SAC AND PAC RESPECTIVELY.  (LOW ORDER PART
012517,000097:                                                                                          	# EQUAL TO ZERO).
012518,000098: 
