060685,000155: 
060686,000156: $AGC_BLOCK_TWO_SELF-CHECK.agc			        # pp. 1394-1403
060688,000002:                                                                                          	## Copyright:   Public domain.
060689,000003:                                                                                          	## Filename:    AGC_BLOCK_TWO_SELF-CHECK.agc
060690,000004:                                                                                          	## Purpose:     Part of the source code for Colossus 2A, AKA Comanche 055.
060691,000005:                                                                                          	##              It is part of the source code for the Command Module's (CM)
060692,000006:                                                                                          	##              Apollo Guidance Computer (AGC), for Apollo 11.
060693,000007:                                                                                          	## Assembler:   yaYUL
060694,000008:                                                                                          	## Contact:     Ron Burkey <info@sandroid.org>.
060695,000009:                                                                                          	## Website:     www.ibiblio.org/apollo.
060696,000010:                                                                                          	## Pages:       1394-1403
060697,000011:                                                                                          	## Mod history: 2009-05-10 SN  (Sergio Navarro).  Started adapting
060698,000012:                                                                                          	##                              from the Colossus249/ file of the same
060699,000013:                                                                                          	##                              name, using Comanche055 page images.
060700,000014:                                                                                          	##              2016-12-22 RSB  Proofed comment text using octopus/ProoferComments
060701,000015:                                                                                          	##                              and corrected the errors found.
060702,000016:                                                                                          	##
060703,000017:                                                                                          	## This source code has been transcribed or otherwise adapted from digitized
060704,000018:                                                                                          	## images of a hardcopy from the MIT Museum.  The digitization was performed
060705,000019:                                                                                          	## by Paul Fjeld, and arranged for by Deborah Douglas of the Museum.  Many
060706,000020:                                                                                          	## thanks to both.  The images (with suitable reduction in storage size and
060707,000021:                                                                                          	## consequent reduction in image quality as well) are available online at
060708,000022:                                                                                          	## www.ibiblio.org/apollo.  If for some reason you find that the images are
060709,000023:                                                                                          	## illegible, contact me at info@sandroid.org about getting access to the
060710,000024:                                                                                          	## (much) higher-quality images which Paul actually created.
060711,000025:                                                                                          	##
060712,000026:                                                                                          	## Notations on the hardcopy document read, in part:
060713,000027:                                                                                          	##
060714,000028:                                                                                          	##    Assemble revision 055 of AGC program Comanche by NASA
060715,000029:                                                                                          	##    2021113-051.  10:28 APR. 1, 1969 
060716,000030:                                                                                          	##
060717,000031:                                                                                          	##    This AGC program shall also be referred to as
060718,000032:                                                                                          	##            Colossus 2A
060719,000033: 
060721,000035:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM DESCRIPTION                           DATE  20 DECEMBER 1967
060722,000036:                                                                                          	# PROGRAM NAME - SELF-CHECK                     LOG SECTION AGC BLOCK TWO SELF-CHECK
060723,000037:                                                                                          	# MOD NO - 1                                    ASSEMBLY SUBROUTINE UTILITYM REV 25
060724,000038:                                                                                          	# MOD BY - GAUNTT
060725,000039: 
060726,000040:                                                                                          	# FUNCTIONAL DESCRIPTION
060727,000041:                                                                                          	#       PROGRAM HAS TWO MAIN PARTS.  THE FIRST IS SELF-CHECK WHICH RUNS AS A ZERO PRIORITY JOB WITH NO CORE SET, AS
060728,000042:                                                                                          	#       PART OF THE BACK-UP IDLE LOOP.  THE SECOND IS SHOW-BANKSUM WHICH RUNS AS A REGULAR EXECUTIVE JOB WITH ITS OWN
060729,000043:                                                                                          	#       STARTING VERB.
060730,000044: 
060731,000045:                                                                                          	#       THE PURPOSE OF SELF-CHECK IS TO CHECK OUT VARIOUS PARTS OF THE COMPUTER AS OUTLINED BELOW IN THE OPTIONS.
060732,000046: 
060733,000047:                                                                                          	#       THE PURPOSE OF SHOW-BANKSUM IS TO DISPLAY THE SUM OF EACH BANK, ONE AT A TIME.
060734,000048: 
060735,000049:                                                                                          	#       IN ALL THERE ARE 7 POSSIBLE OPTIONS IN THIS BLOCK II VERSION OF SELF-CHECK.  MORE DETAIL DESCRIPTION MAY BE
060736,000050:                                                                                          	#       FOUND IN E-2065 BLOCK II AGC SELF-CHECK AND SHOW BANKSUM BY EDWIN D. SMALLY DECEMBER 1966, AND ADDENDA 2 AND 3.
060737,000051: 
060738,000052:                                                                                          	#       THE DIFFERENT OPTIONS ARE CONTROLLED BY PUTTING DIFFERENT NUMBERS IN THE SMODE REGISTER (NOUN 27).  BELOW IS
060739,000053:                                                                                          	#       A DESCRIPTION OF WHAT PARTS OF THE COMPUTER THAT ARE CHECKED BY THE OPTIONS, AND THE CORRESPONDING NUMBER, IN
060740,000054:                                                                                          	#       OCTAL, TO LOAD INTO SMODE.
060741,000055:                                                                                          	#               +-4             ERASABLE MEMORY
060742,000056:                                                                                          	#               +-5             FIXED MEMORY
060743,000057:                                                                                          	#               +-1,2,3,6,7,10  EVERYTHING IN OPTIONS 4 AND 5.
060744,000058:                                                                                          	#               -0              SAME AS +-10 UNTIL AN ERROR IS DETECTED.
060745,000059:                                                                                          	#               +0              NO CHECK, PUTS COMPUTER INTO THE BACKUP IDLE LOOP.
060746,000060: 
060747,000061:                                                                                          	# WARNINGS
060748,000062:                                                                                          	#       USE OF E MEMORY RESERVED FOR SELF-CHECK (EVEN IN IDLE LOOP) AS TEMP STORAGE BY OTHER PROGRAMS IS DANGEROUS.
060749,000063:                                                                                          	#       SMODE SET GREATER THAN OCT 10 PUTS COMPUTER INTO BACKUP IDLE LOOP.
060750,000064: 
060751,000065:                                                                                          	# CALLING SEQUENCE
060752,000066:                                                                                          	#       TO CALL SELF-CHECK KEY IN
060753,000067:                                                                                          	#               V 21 N 27 E     OPTION NUMBER E
060754,000068:                                                                                          	#       TO CALL SHOW-BANKSUM KEY IN
060755,000069:                                                                                          	#               V 91 E          DISPLAYS FIRST BANK
060756,000070:                                                                                          	#               V 33 E          PROCEED, DISPLAYS NEXT BANK
060757,000071: 
060758,000072:                                                                                          	# EXIT MODES, NORMAL AND ALARM
060759,000073:                                                                                          	#       SELF-CHECK NORMALLY CONTINUES INDEFINITELY UNLESS THERE IS AN ERROR DETECTED.  IF SO + OPTION NUMBERS PUT
060760,000074:                                                                                          	#       COMPUTER INTO BACKUP IDLE LOOP, - OPTION NUMBERS RESTART THE OPTION.
060761,000075: 
060762,000076:                                                                                          	#       THE -0 OPTION PROCEEDS FROM THE LINE FOLLOWING THE LINE WHERE THE ERROR WAS DETECTED.
060763,000077: 
060764,000078:                                                                                          	#       SHOW-BANKSUM PROCEEDS UNTIL A TERMINATE IS KEYED IN (V 34 E).  THE COMPUTER IS PUT INTO THE BACKUP IDLE LOOP
060765,000079: 
060766,000080:                                                                                          	# OUTPUT
060768,000082:                                                                                          	#       SELF-CHECK UPON DETECTING AN ERROR LOADS THE SELF-CHECK ALARM CONSTANT (01102) INTO THE FAILREG SET AND
060769,000083:                                                                                          	#       TURNS ON THE ALARM LIGHT.  THE OPERATOR MAY THEN DISPLAY THE THREE FAILREGS BY KEYING IN V 05 N 09 E.  FOR FURTHER
060770,000084:                                                                                          	#       INFORMATION HE MAY KEY IN V 05 N 08 E, THE DSKY DISPLAY IN R1 WILL BE ADDRESS+1 OF WHERE THE ERROR WAS DETECTED,
060771,000085:                                                                                          	#       IN R2 THE BBCON OF SELF-CHECK, AND IN R3 THE TOTAL NUMBER OF ERRORS DETECTED BY SELF-CHECK SINCE THE LAST MAN
060772,000086:                                                                                          	#       INITIATED FRESH START (SLAP1).
060773,000087: 
060774,000088:                                                                                          	#       SHOW-BANKSUM STARTING WITH BANK 0 DISPLAYS IN R1 THE BANK SUM (A +-NUMBER EQUAL TO THE BANK NUMBER), IN R2
060775,000089:                                                                                          	#       THE BANK NUMBER, AND IN R3 THE BUGGER WORD.
060776,000090: 
060777,000091:                                                                                          	# ERASABLE INITIALIZATION REQUIRED
